00:35:06.630 --> 00:35:10.220
for like a month, I guess
or even more and fuck knows

00:35:10.220 --> 00:35:12.980
how I would just get
like normal necessities

00:35:12.980 --> 00:35:15.540
that I just can't find in stores.

00:35:15.540 --> 00:35:18.370
- Right. It's like, oh, you
know, I need a phone charger.

00:35:18.370 --> 00:35:20.660
I couldn't just, you know, go
on Amazon, get it delivered,

00:35:20.660 --> 00:35:21.493
probably the same day.

00:35:21.493 --> 00:35:24.080
Or I could trek 30 minutes
by train to the closest

00:35:24.080 --> 00:35:26.720
big camera to buy one measly cable.

00:35:26.720 --> 00:35:27.970
Why would I do that?

00:35:27.970 --> 00:35:29.450
- Tokyo doesn't have this, but London did.

00:35:29.450 --> 00:35:31.320
London had Amazon now

00:35:31.320 --> 00:35:33.210
and it was basically
like two hour windows.

00:35:33.210 --> 00:35:34.043
- Yeah.

00:35:34.043 --> 00:35:35.410
- You could, if you ordered
it, it would come in two hours.

00:35:35.410 --> 00:35:36.243
- Oh, wow.

00:35:36.243 --> 00:35:37.591
- Yeah, it was pretty good.

00:35:37.591 --> 00:35:38.424
- I was just saying...

00:35:38.424 --> 00:35:39.257
- Like expedited shipping?

00:35:39.257 --> 00:35:42.000
- Yeah, like sometimes we
would be at a house party

00:35:42.000 --> 00:35:44.550
