and like instead of going

00:35:44.550 --> 00:35:47.140
to the Tesco we'd literally
just order our alcohol

00:35:47.140 --> 00:35:50.080
off Amazon and it would just
turn up like an hour later

00:35:50.080 --> 00:35:51.130
when we were like low on beers.

00:35:51.130 --> 00:35:52.512
- Yeah, yeah.

00:35:52.512 --> 00:35:53.345
- This is the future.

00:35:53.345 --> 00:35:54.770
- Yeah, like a whole crate.

00:35:54.770 --> 00:35:56.250
And then also, like I remember
I ordered a crate of beer

00:35:56.250 --> 00:35:59.391
and like a Nintendo switch
game and I was like sick.

00:35:59.391 --> 00:36:00.224
(Garnt and Joey laughing)

00:36:00.224 --> 00:36:01.057
So I was like...

00:36:01.057 --> 00:36:02.147
- They're like who ordered this?

00:36:02.147 --> 00:36:04.980
(Garnt and Joey laughing)

00:36:04.980 --> 00:36:08.343
- Yeah, like who ordered a
fucking Mario Party Super?

00:36:08.343 --> 00:36:11.060
So, Super Mario Party
and I'm like, that's me.

00:36:11.060 --> 00:36:12.500
- It was at the bottom of the box.

00:36:12.500 --> 00:36:14.030
- Just really wanted to play Mario Party.

00:36:14.030 --> 00:36:16.455
- I'm just fucking jealous of the guy

00:36:16.455 --> 00:36:17.288
in the other room playing Mario.

00:36:17.288 --> 00:36:18.300
I really wanted it, man.

00:36:19.170 --> 00:36:20.310
- That's awesome though.

00:36:20.310 --> 00:36:21.143
- I think on that incident,

00:36:21.143 --> 00:36:23.511
it was quicker to get it
delivered on Amazon now,

00:36:23.511 --> 00:36:25.107
than it was to download it.

00:36:25.107 --> 00:36:25.943
- Oh, wow.

00:36:25.943 --> 00:36:27.810
- Because the download is a piece of shit.

00:36:27.810 --> 00:36:29.140
- Oh yeah, yeah, true, true.

00:36:29.140 --> 00:36:31.550
- That's like first world
problems in a nutshell.

00:36:31.550 --> 00:36:34.520
Download too slow, just
order it off Amazon.

00:36:34.520 --> 00:36:35.740
It's slightly faster

00:36:38.491 --> 00:36:41.000
- Because when I used to make long videos,

00:36:41.000 --> 00:36:44.570
I had to leave my PC on all
night and a bit on the next day.

00:36:44.570 --> 00:36:45.613
I couldn't use it.

00:36:46.626 --> 00:36:48.776
I distribute upload
files for Evan to edit,

00:36:50.220 --> 00:36:51.610
I would have to leave it on all night.

00:36:51.610 --> 00:36:53.940
Hoping that when I woke
up, they were all uploaded.

00:36:53.940 --> 00:36:55.910
Otherwise I probably would
be able to use my PC.

00:36:55.910 --> 00:36:56.743
- Right.

00:36:56.743 --> 00:36:57.880
So, yeah, that was a pain in the ass.

00:36:57.880 --> 00:36:59.270
Now I just upload it in one hour.

00:36:59.270 --> 00:37:02.203
- Because that's the one with
the copper wiring, right?

00:37:02.203 --> 00:37:04.040
Is that like when you're
using an upload, for example,

