00:37:12.480 --> 00:37:14.610
I couldn't use the internet
because I had legitimately

00:37:14.610 --> 00:37:15.980
like fucking dial up speed.

00:37:15.980 --> 00:37:18.350
- I was about to say going
back to dial up at this point.

00:37:18.350 --> 00:37:19.992
- It was legitimately dial up speed.

00:37:19.992 --> 00:37:23.110
It took like two minutes
to load up Twitter

00:37:23.110 --> 00:37:24.970
and I'm just like, I
can't, I can't do this.

00:37:24.970 --> 00:37:26.052
- I can't live like this.

00:37:26.052 --> 00:37:26.885
- I can't do this man.

00:37:26.885 --> 00:37:27.790
Why would you do this to me?

00:37:27.790 --> 00:37:28.623
- Yeah, it's crazy.

00:37:28.623 --> 00:37:30.140
And they said like, the
companies used to throttle

00:37:30.140 --> 00:37:31.580
my internet all the fucking time.

00:37:31.580 --> 00:37:33.010
- God, were you a Virgin.

00:37:33.010 --> 00:37:33.843
- Yeah.

00:37:33.843 --> 00:37:34.680
- Fucking virgin man

00:37:34.680 --> 00:37:36.120
- Virgin media fucking sucks.

00:37:36.120 --> 00:37:38.340
- My God, what a version company?

00:37:38.340 --> 00:37:41.870
- They would really have
closed shop because, on paper

00:37:41.870 --> 00:37:44.230
they give you the best internet speeds.

00:37:44.230 --> 00:37:45.420
- 100 megabytes download.

00:37:45.420 --> 00:37:47.530
Never fucking saw it once.

00:37:47.530 --> 00:37:48.363
- You never see it.

00:37:48.363 --> 00:37:52.270
And at peak times, man, you
are not getting anywhere close,

00:37:52.270 --> 00:37:54.902
near to what they advertise to you.

00:37:54.902 --> 00:37:57.090
- The moment you upload or
download anything as well

00:37:57.090 --> 00:37:58.553
they immediately throttle
you and had to call them up

00:37:58.553 --> 00:38:01.460
so many times like,
hey, turn that shit off.

00:38:01.460 --> 00:38:02.423
I paid for this.

00:38:03.419 --> 00:38:05.061
And they charge you so much.

00:38:05.061 --> 00:38:06.130
- We're going back to the days of dial up

00:38:06.130 --> 00:38:08.140
where you have to be like,
mom, get off the phone,

00:38:08.140 --> 00:38:09.510
I'm downloading a game.

00:38:09.510 --> 00:38:10.940
- I had to that to my little brother

00:38:10.940 --> 00:38:12.897
when I used to play league
at home, I'd be like,

00:38:12.897 --> 00:38:16.273
and my ping would go
from like maybe 66, 150.

00:38:17.150 --> 00:38:18.900
I'm like get off the fucking phone.

00:38:21.289 --> 00:38:24.870
- I remember back in university,
whenever you were living

00:38:24.870 --> 00:38:26.090
in like a shared house, my God,

00:38:26.090 --> 00:38:29.810
trying to game in a shared
house is fucking impossible.

00:38:29.810 --> 00:38:33.920
Cause yeah, your ping
would either be like 10,

00:38:33.920 --> 00:38:36.733
when no one's awake or
when it's dinner time,

00:38:36.733 --> 00:38:38.560
it's like fucking 800.

00:38:38.560 --> 00:38:40.610
I'm like, who's fucking downloading

00:38:40.610 --> 00:38:42.180
another episode of 'Game of Thrones'.

00:38:42.180 --> 00:38:43.400
Everyone's a fucking duck.

00:38:43.400 --> 00:38:44.573
Everyone's torrenting.

00:38:45.416 --> 00:38:46.249
- Everyone puts their hands up.

00:38:48.000 --> 00:38:50.360
- It was fucking worse for me because

00:38:50.360 --> 00:38:52.890
when I was doing YouTube,
like way back in Australia,

00:38:52.890 --> 00:38:55.170
all of my YouTuber friends
were in America, right?

00:38:55.170 --> 00:38:57.270
So every time I'd jumped onto
like G-mode or something,

00:38:57.270 --> 00:38:59.960
on a good day, my ping would be like 300.

00:38:59.960 --> 00:39:00.880
I'd be like, guys...

00:39:00.880 --> 00:39:02.900
- Why even play a 300 pings?

00:39:02.900 --> 00:39:05.179
- Cause I was desperate for friends.

00:39:05.179 --> 00:39:06.576
(Garnt and Joey laughing)

00:39:06.576 --> 00:39:09.930
I didn't have any YouTuber
friends in Australia.

00:39:09.930 --> 00:39:13.230
- There must be a Formula
for like ping correlation

00:39:13.230 --> 00:39:16.100
with how desperate you are
to hang out with that person.

00:39:16.100 --> 00:39:18.429
Because I play league of legends
a lot with Titus and Emily

00:39:18.429 --> 00:39:19.262
and it's like 200 ping.

00:39:19.262 --> 00:39:22.670
And I'm like, man, this
sucks, but it's really fun.

00:39:22.670 --> 00:39:26.190
- Oh yeah, I mean 300
pings G-mode was still fun.

00:39:26.190 --> 00:39:28.010
But I mean, yeah, no one could kill me

00:39:28.010 --> 00:39:30.010
because I just keep fucking teleporting.

00:39:31.030 --> 00:39:33.860
- What is the value of friendship, right?

00:39:33.860 --> 00:39:35.490
- Is it 300 pings.

00:39:35.490 --> 00:39:37.003
- What is your ping limit for us?

00:39:37.003 --> 00:39:38.100
- We should break down
the value of friendship

00:39:38.100 --> 00:39:39.275
by ping number.

00:39:39.275 --> 00:39:40.108
(Joey laughs)

00:39:40.108 --> 00:39:41.820
Like, would I pay 160 ping for you?

00:39:41.820 --> 00:39:43.160
Yeah, I'll pay you for that.

00:39:43.160 --> 00:39:44.613
- 800 ping, ultimate friend.

00:39:45.770 --> 00:39:47.793
100 ping, just an acquaintance.

00:39:47.793 --> 00:39:49.790
- I just wanna talk to you, man.

00:39:49.790 --> 00:39:51.500
- Yeah, so you used to upload daily

00:39:51.500 --> 00:39:52.690
on that garbage internet.

00:39:52.690 --> 00:39:53.523
- I sure did.

00:39:53.523 --> 00:39:54.658
- Oh my God.

00:39:54.658 --> 00:39:56.261
- And that's why my
computer exploded, remember?

00:39:56.261 --> 00:39:57.840
- How did you not get like
burned out, from that.

00:39:57.840 --> 00:39:58.740
I think I would like hey,...

00:39:58.740 --> 00:40:00.290
- I mean, I did get burned out,

00:40:01.255 --> 00:40:03.950
after like two and a
half years of doing that.

00:40:03.950 --> 00:40:07.970
Because I quit Let's Plays a
week before I moved to Japan.

00:40:07.970 --> 00:40:11.650
- I remember when you quit
that and I thought like, good.

00:40:11.650 --> 00:40:13.800
- Yeah, everyone was like, good.

00:40:13.800 --> 00:40:14.970
You should have done that.

00:40:14.970 --> 00:40:16.400
And I think I did it at the perfect time

00:40:16.400 --> 00:40:19.830
because that was just around
the time, like early 2015.

00:40:19.830 --> 00:40:21.320
That was around the time when gaming

00:40:21.320 --> 00:40:22.700
was kind of starting to dip.

00:40:22.700 --> 00:40:23.680
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:40:23.680 --> 00:40:24.610
- Like just overall, that's when YouTube

00:40:24.610 --> 00:40:25.900
kind of shafted all of gaming.

00:40:25.900 --> 00:40:28.580
YouTube was like no
more spotlight for you.

00:40:28.580 --> 00:40:30.410
- Yeah, that's around 2015.

00:40:30.410 --> 00:40:32.670
- Which like speaking
about that, have you guys

00:40:32.670 --> 00:40:36.290
in your YouTube careers, ever
properly experienced burnout?

00:40:36.290 --> 00:40:37.357
- Oh yeah.

00:40:37.357 --> 00:40:40.980
- When was the last time you
guys experienced burnout?

00:40:40.980 --> 00:40:44.680
- Last time I experienced
like proper burnout was maybe,

00:40:44.680 --> 00:40:46.630
this was back before I
was leaving with Aki.

00:40:46.630 --> 00:40:47.742
- [Garnt] Right.

00:40:47.742 --> 00:40:49.045
- And I was just living on my own.

00:40:49.045 --> 00:40:51.700
And yeah, I just had like a moment,

00:40:51.700 --> 00:40:54.850
like maybe for like half a year
where I was just constantly,

00:40:54.850 --> 00:40:56.390
like all I was thinking
about was like, all right.

00:40:56.390 --> 00:40:57.230
What's the next video?

00:40:57.230 --> 00:40:58.713
What's the next one?

00:40:58.713 --> 00:40:59.546
I just keep one upping myself.

00:40:59.546 --> 00:41:02.129
And like just coming up with
ideas because even back then,

00:41:02.129 --> 00:41:03.797
I think it was maybe uploading like once

00:41:03.797 --> 00:41:05.520
every three days or something.

00:41:05.520 --> 00:41:09.620
So not as intense as daily
but it's still pretty intense.

00:41:09.620 --> 00:41:12.117
Especially because now I wasn't
doing Let's Plays anymore.

00:41:12.117 --> 00:41:13.340
I was doing like straight up like,

00:41:13.340 --> 00:41:16.140
I was writing a script every fucking day.

00:41:16.140 --> 00:41:19.050
So that shit burnt me
out like a hell of a lot.

00:41:19.050 --> 00:41:21.300
And there was like a point
where I was legitimately like,

00:41:21.300 --> 00:41:23.239
should I just like stop?

00:41:23.239 --> 00:41:25.050
Like, should I just stop
YouTube for a while?

00:41:25.050 --> 00:41:25.883
- Yeah.

00:41:25.883 --> 00:41:27.793
- But then I was like,
nah, ain't worth it.

00:41:28.760 --> 00:41:30.900
- I think a lot of
people view us here a lot

00:41:30.900 --> 00:41:34.234
about like, the mystical
YouTube burnout, what it means,

00:41:34.234 --> 00:41:36.540
like, can you like try to explain.

00:41:36.540 --> 00:41:40.860
- At this point, I'm sure
for a viewer hearing burnout

00:41:42.764 --> 00:41:44.120
was just like, oh let's just get that

00:41:44.120 --> 00:41:46.010
off the YouTuber checklist.

00:41:46.010 --> 00:41:49.520
It's kind of just become a cliche now.

00:41:49.520 --> 00:41:51.200
It's like, oh, you reached burnout.

00:41:51.200 --> 00:41:52.033
Okay, okay.

00:41:52.033 --> 00:41:54.340
- All right, see you in a couple of days,

00:41:54.340 --> 00:41:55.710
you'll be over it soon.

00:41:55.710 --> 00:41:58.710
Like people think that
YouTuber burnout is just like,

00:41:58.710 --> 00:41:59.543
like I dunno

00:41:59.543 --> 00:42:00.376
- Woe is me.

00:42:00.376 --> 00:42:01.550
- Yeah, kind of a woe is me,

00:42:01.550 --> 00:42:03.760
like a very privileged
first-world problem.

00:42:03.760 --> 00:42:07.199
But I think it's just another
form of like creative burnout.

00:42:07.199 --> 00:42:10.440
And if you've never experienced
burnout in your life

00:42:10.440 --> 00:42:13.180
or create a burnout, artists
block is another word for it.

00:42:13.180 --> 00:42:15.700
It's essentially where
you want to do something

00:42:15.700 --> 00:42:17.720
and you want to make
something, but you either

00:42:17.720 --> 00:42:20.340
have no motivation or
no inspiration to do,

00:42:20.340 --> 00:42:21.173
or both sometimes.

00:42:21.173 --> 00:42:24.640
You're just like, man, I
really want to get a video out.

00:42:24.640 --> 00:42:26.020
I know I need to get a video out.

00:42:26.020 --> 00:42:27.490
I want to be creative.

00:42:27.490 --> 00:42:28.710
I just don't know what to do.

00:42:28.710 --> 00:42:29.543
- Yeah.

00:42:29.543 --> 00:42:30.376
- And I have no motivation for it.

00:42:30.376 --> 00:42:31.253
- Yeah.

00:42:31.253 --> 00:42:33.170
I think there's one person
who reached burnout recently.

00:42:33.170 --> 00:42:35.470
Then they made a statement about it

00:42:35.470 --> 00:42:38.180
and like hit me hard because...

00:42:38.180 --> 00:42:42.670
So the author of "Tower of
God" recently went on hiatus

00:42:42.670 --> 00:42:45.180
for like an indefinite period of time.

00:42:45.180 --> 00:42:47.290
So we don't know, he hasn't said,

00:42:47.290 --> 00:42:48.720
I'm going to be away for this long.

00:42:48.720 --> 00:42:52.310
He actually just wrote like
a really really long post

00:42:52.310 --> 00:42:55.590
just detailing that
he's just had no breaks

00:42:55.590 --> 00:42:58.500
for this entire like time
during "Tower of gods".

00:42:58.500 --> 00:43:01.170
And I remember there was
one line that really hit me

00:43:01.170 --> 00:43:04.060
which was, I think he said, I didn't know

00:43:04.060 --> 00:43:07.170
whether I was working to
upload or uploading to work.

00:43:07.170 --> 00:43:08.003
No, no.

00:43:08.003 --> 00:43:10.060
I didn't know whether
I was living to upload

00:43:10.060 --> 00:43:11.150
or upload to live.

00:43:11.150 --> 00:43:12.928
You know what I mean?

00:43:12.928 --> 00:43:14.940
And I'm just like, dude,
I totally get that, man.

00:43:14.940 --> 00:43:16.521
- [Joey] Yeah, yeah.

00:43:16.521 --> 00:43:17.650
- Because there are times during burnout

00:43:17.650 --> 00:43:19.126
where you're just like, man

00:43:19.126 --> 00:43:20.280
- What am you doing?

00:43:20.280 --> 00:43:21.113
- What am I doing?

00:43:21.113 --> 00:43:22.610
Am I even enjoying this anymore?

00:43:22.610 --> 00:43:24.900
- So I mean, to explain to the viewers,

00:43:24.900 --> 00:43:26.920
how do you like get into burnout?

00:43:26.920 --> 00:43:29.782
Like, how do you, like,
what does it feel like?

00:43:29.782 --> 00:43:31.290
Like, like how does it start?

00:43:31.290 --> 00:43:32.840
- It happens in so many different ways.

00:43:32.840 --> 00:43:35.750
I feel really depends
on the person, but like,

00:43:35.750 --> 00:43:39.073
a common thing that would
happen is, for example,

00:43:40.070 --> 00:43:42.490
like if you uploaded
like four or five videos

00:43:42.490 --> 00:43:44.670
that are like absolute bangers, right.

00:43:44.670 --> 00:43:46.680
It's just like, boom, views,
boom views, boom, views.

00:43:46.680 --> 00:43:49.540
And then after that really good streak

00:43:49.540 --> 00:43:52.280
you have another streak, but
in the opposite direction

00:43:52.280 --> 00:43:53.750
of like, oh, that one bombed, oh,

00:43:53.750 --> 00:43:54.600
that one bombed even harder.

00:43:54.600 --> 00:43:56.210
Oh, that one bombed even harder.

00:43:56.210 --> 00:44:00.870
And you start to lose self
motivation and like you start to,

00:44:00.870 --> 00:44:02.690
I dunno, it's really hard
to explain, isn't it?

00:44:02.690 --> 00:44:06.350
You don't realize creative burnout started

00:44:06.350 --> 00:44:07.730
until you're deep in creative burnout.

00:44:07.730 --> 00:44:10.500
- Yeah, it's really hard
to see the early signs

00:44:10.500 --> 00:44:11.333
of creative burnout.

00:44:11.333 --> 00:44:14.220
Sometimes it's just, you just
wake up and you just do a job.

00:44:14.220 --> 00:44:15.977
And then eventually like
five months down the line

00:44:15.977 --> 00:44:18.950
you're like, man, I've
just been feeling the same.

00:44:18.950 --> 00:44:20.960
Exactly the same this entire five months.

00:44:20.960 --> 00:44:23.466
And I'm just not getting
anything new out of this.

00:44:23.466 --> 00:44:27.960
- I'm sure, like most people
who just work normal jobs

00:44:27.960 --> 00:44:29.320
get it as well with their own job

00:44:29.320 --> 00:44:31.536
where they just kind of feel light,

00:44:31.536 --> 00:44:33.630
like, hmm, do I like this or?

00:44:33.630 --> 00:44:35.640
Like, I know a lot of people
don't like what they do

00:44:35.640 --> 00:44:36.600
and they just do it to survive

00:44:36.600 --> 00:44:38.147
because they don't have a choice.

00:44:38.147 --> 00:44:41.530
I mean, we're very lucky
